1
00:00:01,501 --> 00:00:02,793
"Previously
on the mentalist..."

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:06,339
"Ten years ago, the serial killer
known as Red John"

3
00:00:06,464 --> 00:00:08,049
"Killed my wife and daughter."

4
00:00:12,553 --> 00:00:15,223
"We've been hunting
for him ever since."

5
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:17,433
We call ourselves
the Blake association.

6
00:00:17,808 --> 00:00:19,393
"Well, who else
is in the association?"

7
00:00:19,602 --> 00:00:21,395
Cops, judges, FBI agents...

8
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:24,190
Anyone in law enforcement
that needs a secret covered up.

9
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:26,234
A secret society
of dirty cops.

10
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,110
And Red John's a member.

11
00:00:29,028 --> 00:00:32,198
Kira Tinsley told me something
before she passed.

12
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:34,742
She told me that her killer...
Red John...

13
00:00:34,867 --> 00:00:36,035
Has a tattoo...

14
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:38,829
Three dots on his left arm.

15
00:00:39,747 --> 00:00:40,831
So who's Red John?

16
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:42,166
Today we're pleased
to announce

17
00:00:42,291 --> 00:00:45,503
That we...we finally have
a name, a face.

18
00:00:46,754 --> 00:00:48,923
The director of the division
of law enforcement

19
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:51,551
Gail Bertram, is Red John.

20
00:00:51,884 --> 00:00:55,179
I am holding in my hand
a writ

21
00:00:55,429 --> 00:00:56,722
from a federal judge.

22
00:00:56,973 --> 00:01:00,726
The FBI is closing down
your organization right now.

23
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:03,354
We're done. There's
nothing more to do here.

24
00:01:03,771 --> 00:01:06,148
"You're not quitting.
I don't believe it."

25
00:01:06,357 --> 00:01:07,692
It's out of our hands
for now.

26
00:01:08,484 --> 00:01:10,319
I'll be in touch. Okay?

27
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:13,948
I'm sorry.
For everything.

28
00:01:42,351 --> 00:01:43,394
Lisbon.

29
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:46,063
Glad you can join us.

30
00:01:46,522 --> 00:01:49,692
- Traffic.
- Hmm. Where's Jane?

31
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:52,236
He'll be in to see you
as soon as he's able.

32
00:01:53,571 --> 00:01:54,614
This way.

33
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:08,878
Please, take a seat.

34
00:02:13,257 --> 00:02:14,759
Boy, this is a mess, huh?

35
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:17,762
A big mess.

36
00:02:17,887 --> 00:02:19,388
- Look, I think we all...
- you can talk later.

37
00:02:21,766 --> 00:02:23,392
Now I understand...

38
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,896
You must all feel scared

39
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:28,856
Nervous.

40
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:31,776
Don't know what in the hell
is gonna happen next, right?

41
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:33,861
- Agent...
- so let me explain what's next.

42
00:02:37,531 --> 00:02:38,699
Over the next few days

43
00:02:38,824 --> 00:02:40,993
we will be talking
to each of you...

44
00:02:41,243 --> 00:02:42,286
individually.

45
00:02:43,162 --> 00:02:45,289
You are entitled to bring along
an attorney

46
00:02:45,915 --> 00:02:49,085
or a union rep,
should you so choose.

47
00:02:49,251 --> 00:02:50,711
Why would we need an attorney?

48
00:02:52,588 --> 00:02:55,591
Well, let's look at this
from our perspective, Kimball.

49
00:02:56,217 --> 00:02:58,344
Your boss Bertram
is a criminal.

50
00:02:59,136 --> 00:03:01,097
Makes sense that you
might be one, too.

51
00:03:02,264 --> 00:03:05,267
We will be looking very closely
at all of you.

52
00:03:05,393 --> 00:03:07,687
If you have ever done anything

53
00:03:07,978 --> 00:03:09,939
even remotely questionable

54
00:03:10,981 --> 00:03:12,316
we will find out

55
00:03:12,733 --> 00:03:14,235
and we will prosecute.

56
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,571
Unless, of course

57
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:21,742
we feel very, very comfortable
with your cooperation.

58
00:03:22,576 --> 00:03:24,829
Then you got
a little wiggle room.

59
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:33,921
"The FBI is overseeing"

60
00:03:34,046 --> 00:03:35,506
"an international manhunt"

61
00:03:35,631 --> 00:03:38,259
"for prominent Sacramento
law enforcement official"

62
00:03:38,467 --> 00:03:39,510
"Gail Bertram."

63
00:03:39,635 --> 00:03:41,303
"FBI sources confirm
that Bertram"

64
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:44,682
"is believed to be the notorious
serial killer Red John"

65
00:03:45,015 --> 00:03:46,726
"wanted for a string
of grisly murders"

66
00:03:46,851 --> 00:03:48,769
"across
the California heartland."

67
00:04:07,747 --> 00:04:08,789
Hey, man.

68
00:04:08,914 --> 00:04:10,124
How's it going?

69
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:19,383
Do you have a pay phone?

70
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:20,968
It's right back there.

71
00:04:24,889 --> 00:04:25,931
Thank you.

72
00:04:33,731 --> 00:04:36,108
Hey, Ali, how you doing?
Uh, give me a pick 6...

73
00:04:36,233 --> 00:04:38,194
and one of those
pineapple cheroots.

74
00:04:39,695 --> 00:04:42,448
Pick 6. Cheroot.

75
00:05:02,676 --> 00:05:03,719
Hello?

76
00:05:03,844 --> 00:05:04,887
"Hello, Patrick."

77
00:05:06,222 --> 00:05:07,723
I don't have to use
a funny voice, do I?

78
00:05:07,848 --> 00:05:09,016
You know who this is.

79
00:05:09,141 --> 00:05:10,184
Yes, I do.

80
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:12,269
It's weird, huh?

81
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:14,355
'cause the last time we...

82
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:22,404
Put your hands up...

83
00:05:31,497 --> 00:05:32,540
"Hello?"

84
00:05:35,584 --> 00:05:37,253
- "Hello?"
- Thanks.

85
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:41,215
- No problem.
- "Hello? Bertram? Hello?"

86
00:06:25,424 --> 00:06:26,592
{\an8}Clear, sir.

87
00:06:28,552 --> 00:06:29,678
No kidding.

88
00:06:47,029 --> 00:06:48,071
{\an8}Where is he?

89
00:06:49,781 --> 00:06:51,783
{\an8}If you're asking about Jane,
I don't know.

90
00:06:52,409 --> 00:06:53,827
{\an8}- Hmm.
- Did you check upstairs?

91
00:06:54,286 --> 00:06:55,329
Yeah.

92
00:06:56,246 --> 00:06:58,332
{\an8}You know, maybe
you haven't heard.

93
00:06:58,957 --> 00:07:00,876
{\an8}About an hour ago,
Gail Bertram

94
00:07:01,168 --> 00:07:03,921
{\an8}Killed a cop at a gas station
in East Sac.

95
00:07:04,338 --> 00:07:05,380
I heard.

96
00:07:06,506 --> 00:07:09,051
{\an8}Did you hear what Bertram was
doing at the gas station?

97
00:07:09,468 --> 00:07:10,510
No.

98
00:07:10,969 --> 00:07:12,220
{\an8}Using a pay phone.

99
00:07:13,388 --> 00:07:14,806
{\an8}Guess who he was calling.

100
00:07:15,432 --> 00:07:16,683
I'm gonna guess Jane.

101
00:07:16,934 --> 00:07:19,811
{\an8}Ahh. Yeah. So where is he?

102
00:07:20,103 --> 00:07:21,146
I don't know.

103
00:07:21,813 --> 00:07:22,981
{\an8}I think you do.

104
00:07:23,315 --> 00:07:25,067
{\an8}I can't help
what you think.

105
00:07:26,151 --> 00:07:27,903
{\an8}I think your boyfriend
is colluding

106
00:07:28,028 --> 00:07:29,404
{\an8}With a dangerous fugitive.

107
00:07:29,613 --> 00:07:31,782
{\an8}I think
he is up to his neck

108
00:07:31,907 --> 00:07:33,617
{\an8}In this Blake association
craziness

109
00:07:33,867 --> 00:07:35,118
and probably you are, too.

110
00:07:35,869 --> 00:07:37,955
{\an8}I'm not. He's not.

111
00:07:38,622 --> 00:07:40,707
{\an8}Jane can't help
who calls him

112
00:07:41,041 --> 00:07:42,584
{\an8}and he's not my boyfriend.

113
00:07:43,001 --> 00:07:44,503
It's a damn shame, Teresa.

114
00:07:46,004 --> 00:07:47,214
{\an8}By all accounts...

115
00:07:47,881 --> 00:07:49,174
you were a good cop.

116
00:07:49,549 --> 00:07:50,592
I still am.

117
00:08:07,109 --> 00:08:08,151
"Hey, boss!"

118
00:08:09,444 --> 00:08:10,487
Rigsby?

119
00:08:11,363 --> 00:08:12,406
Is it safe?

120
00:08:12,656 --> 00:08:13,865
Yeah. What are you doing?

121
00:08:18,745 --> 00:08:20,122
{\an8}We heard about what Bertram
did this morning.

122
00:08:20,247 --> 00:08:21,915
{\an8}We heard the FBI
were looking for us.

123
00:08:22,124 --> 00:08:24,418
So what now? You're hiding
in the parking lot?

124
00:08:24,668 --> 00:08:27,379
No. No, we're not hiding.
We're just... Laying low.

125
00:08:27,546 --> 00:08:29,297
Well, we're safe for now.
There's no arrest warrant

126
00:08:29,423 --> 00:08:30,632
that's put out for us
just yet.

127
00:08:30,757 --> 00:08:31,800
Give 'em time.

128
00:08:31,925 --> 00:08:33,176
Where's Jane?

129
00:08:33,301 --> 00:08:34,761
- Don't ask.
- She just did.

130
00:08:36,555 --> 00:08:37,597
Listen to me.

131
00:08:37,848 --> 00:08:40,017
The C.B.I. is gone now.

132
00:08:40,475 --> 00:08:42,936
{\an8}We're on our own. You need
to protect yourselves.

133
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:45,647
You don't know where Jane is,
you don't know what he's doing

134
00:08:45,772 --> 00:08:48,025
and you don't wanna know,
you understand?

135
00:08:48,734 --> 00:08:49,776
Yes, boss.

136
00:08:51,111 --> 00:08:52,320
- Yes, boss.
- Yes, boss.

137
00:08:52,696 --> 00:08:53,905
All right then.

138
00:08:54,197 --> 00:08:57,075
But I am not your boss anymore.
That's the point.

139
00:08:57,284 --> 00:08:58,326
We're on our own.

140
00:09:00,328 --> 00:09:01,413
Yeah, we get it.

141
00:09:01,955 --> 00:09:03,165
So where is he?

142
00:09:13,467 --> 00:09:14,509
Hey.

143
00:09:14,968 --> 00:09:16,011
Hey.

144
00:09:17,554 --> 00:09:18,597
You're a wanted man.

145
00:09:19,014 --> 00:09:20,307
Well, I like to think so.

146
00:09:20,766 --> 00:09:23,852
Seriously. Abbott put
an actual warrant out on you.

147
00:09:24,061 --> 00:09:25,604
Eh. It's not the first time.

148
00:09:28,065 --> 00:09:29,483
So you gonna tell me,
or what?

149
00:09:29,941 --> 00:09:31,985
Oh, yeah. Uh...
Bertram called me.

150
00:09:32,110 --> 00:09:33,528
- I know.
- Mm.

151
00:09:33,653 --> 00:09:34,696
What did he say?

152
00:09:34,821 --> 00:09:36,656
Well, whatever he wanted to say,
he didn't have time.

153
00:09:38,325 --> 00:09:39,951
Why the hell is he still here?

154
00:09:40,077 --> 00:09:41,161
What does he want?

155
00:09:41,328 --> 00:09:43,580
I'm guessing he'll call back
soon and tell me.

156
00:09:43,914 --> 00:09:45,040
Your phone's not safe.
The FBI...

157
00:09:45,165 --> 00:09:47,125
Yeah, they have a tap
on the line.

158
00:09:47,250 --> 00:09:48,335
But they don't have
a trace yet.

159
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:50,879
If they had a trace,
then I'd be arrested already.

160
00:09:51,004 --> 00:09:53,340
Maybe so, but sooner or later,
they'll get a trace on you.

161
00:09:53,507 --> 00:09:54,549
I know.

162
00:09:54,674 --> 00:09:56,885
But I can't get rid of my phone
until Bertram calls.

163
00:09:57,636 --> 00:09:59,471
It's all very suspenseful.

164
00:10:00,222 --> 00:10:02,057
- What does he want?
- Who?

165
00:10:02,641 --> 00:10:04,309
- Bertram.
- We'll see.

166
00:10:04,768 --> 00:10:05,977
Now you're being evasive.

167
00:10:08,188 --> 00:10:10,398
What beady little eyes
birds have.

168
00:10:11,191 --> 00:10:12,442
Tiny dinosaurs, you know?

169
00:10:12,567 --> 00:10:13,610
I know.

170
00:10:14,861 --> 00:10:16,363
I know you know
what he wants.

171
00:10:16,488 --> 00:10:17,614
What does he want?

172
00:10:22,619 --> 00:10:23,662
Hello?

173
00:10:23,787 --> 00:10:24,830
"Oh, sorry I had to
hang up on you."

174
00:10:24,955 --> 00:10:26,289
It's been a busy day.

175
00:10:26,748 --> 00:10:28,792
Yeah, no problem. You know,
this phone is not safe.

176
00:10:28,917 --> 00:10:30,377
Let me call you back
in a moment.

177
00:10:30,794 --> 00:10:31,837
Yeah.

178
00:10:32,796 --> 00:10:33,839
What'd he say?

179
00:10:33,964 --> 00:10:35,006
Just a second.

180
00:10:35,757 --> 00:10:36,925
Hey. How you doing?

181
00:10:37,884 --> 00:10:40,178
- I'll give you $100 for that phone.
- Huh?

182
00:10:42,848 --> 00:10:44,975
$200 for that phone.

183
00:10:46,268 --> 00:10:47,310
What's the catch?

184
00:10:47,477 --> 00:10:48,562
No catch.

185
00:10:49,437 --> 00:10:51,857
$300 plus...

186
00:10:52,524 --> 00:10:53,817
A replacement phone.

187
00:10:54,901 --> 00:10:55,944
Uh, okay.

188
00:10:56,570 --> 00:10:57,779
Yeah, dude, I'll call you
right back.

189
00:10:58,780 --> 00:11:00,323
Pleasure doing business
with you.

190
00:11:01,366 --> 00:11:02,409
Thanks, man.

191
00:11:02,617 --> 00:11:03,827
Mm-hmm.

192
00:11:05,245 --> 00:11:06,538
What did he say?

193
00:11:06,872 --> 00:11:07,914
Hello?

194
00:11:08,373 --> 00:11:10,125
"Look, I think we should
meet and talk."

195
00:11:10,625 --> 00:11:13,003
- Just the two of us.
- What, like a date?

196
00:11:14,588 --> 00:11:15,881
Yes...

197
00:11:16,256 --> 00:11:17,299
No.

198
00:11:17,591 --> 00:11:20,010
Look, the game is over.

199
00:11:21,928 --> 00:11:25,223
I'd call it
a very honorable tie.

200
00:11:25,724 --> 00:11:27,517
"And now that it's over"

201
00:11:27,893 --> 00:11:29,978
"I really think that
we should talk."

202
00:11:30,395 --> 00:11:32,981
You know, a truce.
No weapons, no tricks.

203
00:11:33,356 --> 00:11:34,399
Just talk.

204
00:11:34,816 --> 00:11:36,151
Then we both walk away.

205
00:11:36,359 --> 00:11:38,361
Talk. About what?

206
00:11:39,321 --> 00:11:41,448
Well... Everything.

207
00:11:41,948 --> 00:11:44,242
I think we both could use
a little closure, don't you?

208
00:11:45,243 --> 00:11:47,787
It has to be today.
You know, now.

209
00:11:48,413 --> 00:11:49,706
I'm kind of
pressed for time.

210
00:11:49,873 --> 00:11:51,208
How do I know I can trust you?

211
00:11:51,416 --> 00:11:53,501
Ah, don't be timid now, Patrick.

212
00:11:54,085 --> 00:11:57,631
I could have Killed you many
times, and I haven't, have I?

213
00:11:57,797 --> 00:12:00,342
Okay. When and where?

214
00:12:00,967 --> 00:12:02,010
Excellent.

215
00:12:02,177 --> 00:12:04,721
I'll be at the Fremont Park
fountain in half an hour.

216
00:12:04,846 --> 00:12:07,474
No. Don't know it.
Central bus station.

217
00:12:07,933 --> 00:12:09,893
- "North entrance."
- Nah, there's too many people.

218
00:12:10,018 --> 00:12:11,061
There's too many cops.

219
00:12:11,269 --> 00:12:12,896
You know Alexandria Cemetery?

220
00:12:14,022 --> 00:12:15,106
Of course I do.

221
00:12:15,690 --> 00:12:17,901
Yeah, there's a chapel
by the western gate.

222
00:12:18,235 --> 00:12:20,570
That...that'll do.
Half an hour.

223
00:12:20,695 --> 00:12:22,239
Don't be late.
I can't wait around.

224
00:12:22,530 --> 00:12:23,573
Half an hour.

225
00:12:26,201 --> 00:12:27,285
What'd he say?

226
00:12:28,828 --> 00:12:30,205
He wants to meet with me.

227
00:12:30,538 --> 00:12:31,581
It's a trap.

228
00:12:32,290 --> 00:12:33,333
Probably.

229
00:12:34,251 --> 00:12:35,418
Well, what are you
gonna do?

230
00:12:37,003 --> 00:12:39,339
- I'm gonna meet him.
- You can't.

231
00:12:40,006 --> 00:12:42,008
Trust me,
I know what I'm doing.

232
00:12:42,175 --> 00:12:44,761
Jane, don't do this.
Think about it.

233
00:12:44,886 --> 00:12:47,097
The FBI is gonna get
Bertram soon enough.

234
00:12:47,222 --> 00:12:49,099
I don't want the FBI
to get him.

235
00:12:51,101 --> 00:12:52,769
You knew this day
was coming.

236
00:12:54,229 --> 00:12:55,355
It's here.

237
00:12:56,189 --> 00:12:58,650
- Let me come with you.
- No, I don't want you involved.

238
00:12:58,775 --> 00:13:01,069
- Involved? I am involved.
- Not anymore.

239
00:13:05,573 --> 00:13:07,117
I'm gonna need
to borrow your gun.

240
00:13:08,952 --> 00:13:09,995
My gun?

241
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:12,330
Yes, your gun. I'm not gonna use it.
Just a prop.

242
00:13:14,499 --> 00:13:17,377
Teresa, trust me, please.
Just trust me.

243
00:13:32,559 --> 00:13:33,601
Thank you.

244
00:13:55,373 --> 00:13:56,541
Like that way.

245
00:13:56,833 --> 00:13:57,917
Thanks.

246
00:15:22,792 --> 00:15:25,294
Where's the man in charge here?
Where is Abbott?

247
00:15:25,420 --> 00:15:27,630
Get down on your knees. Keep your hands
where I can see them.

248
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:29,590
Where is Abbott?
I-I have to go.

249
00:15:29,715 --> 00:15:32,135
All right, take it down
a notch, people.

250
00:15:33,010 --> 00:15:34,429
He's not al Capone.

251
00:15:34,679 --> 00:15:36,264
Abbott, please listen to me.

252
00:15:36,848 --> 00:15:38,683
I can tell that you're
a man of honor.

253
00:15:39,183 --> 00:15:41,727
On my honor, I will
give myself up in an hour.

254
00:15:41,978 --> 00:15:45,440
But right now I just...
I just need...

255
00:15:46,691 --> 00:15:47,775
Just...

256
00:15:51,028 --> 00:15:52,071
Forget it.

257
00:15:52,196 --> 00:15:54,115
No. No, no, no, no.
No, tell me.

258
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:55,283
Come on.

259
00:15:55,408 --> 00:15:57,034
No, what do you need?
What do you need, huh?

260
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,369
You need an hour?

261
00:15:59,078 --> 00:16:00,121
For what?

262
00:16:00,746 --> 00:16:01,914
Where are you going?

263
00:16:02,707 --> 00:16:04,083
Who are you gonna go meet?

264
00:16:05,835 --> 00:16:06,878
No?

265
00:16:07,003 --> 00:16:08,880
Well, let's take a trip
downtown, shall we?

266
00:16:10,339 --> 00:16:11,382
Hey.

267
00:16:11,883 --> 00:16:12,925
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

268
00:16:13,050 --> 00:16:14,260
No. You can let her go.

269
00:16:15,636 --> 00:16:16,721
Hi, Miss Lisbon.

270
00:16:17,430 --> 00:16:19,557
Do me this one favor,
Abbott, cop to cop.

271
00:16:19,682 --> 00:16:22,518
Let him go, and I swear
I will bring him back later.

272
00:16:23,769 --> 00:16:24,812
Not happening.

273
00:16:26,230 --> 00:16:29,233
And what is all this urgency
I'm hearing here? Hmm?

274
00:16:30,193 --> 00:16:32,487
Oh. You made a plan
with Bertram.

275
00:16:33,237 --> 00:16:35,364
Is that it?
Is that what you did?

276
00:16:35,948 --> 00:16:37,074
Please, Abbott.

277
00:16:37,533 --> 00:16:38,784
FBI! Back it off!

278
00:16:38,951 --> 00:16:41,329
- CBI. Back it up yourself.
- What's this?

279
00:16:41,954 --> 00:16:44,040
Let him go, Abbott.
He's done nothing wrong.

280
00:16:45,041 --> 00:16:46,501
Hey, guys.

281
00:16:46,751 --> 00:16:48,211
You know, I... it's good
to see you.

282
00:16:48,544 --> 00:16:51,797
I hate to bring you down,
but there is no CBI.

283
00:16:52,298 --> 00:16:54,133
That badge is a toy

284
00:16:54,717 --> 00:16:57,011
and you're all impersonating
officers of the law.

285
00:16:57,261 --> 00:16:59,096
Whatever. Let him go.

286
00:17:01,849 --> 00:17:03,476
Are you mad-dogging me
right now?

287
00:17:04,185 --> 00:17:05,269
The FBI?

288
00:17:05,728 --> 00:17:07,688
You say you're legit FBI,
but how do we know?

289
00:17:07,813 --> 00:17:09,357
Yeah, you could be members
of the Blake association

290
00:17:09,482 --> 00:17:10,525
for all we know.

291
00:17:11,859 --> 00:17:12,902
We're not.

292
00:17:13,027 --> 00:17:14,070
Prove it.

293
00:17:14,695 --> 00:17:17,240
Your man Reede smith
was a member. Why not you?

294
00:17:18,616 --> 00:17:20,493
And how do we know
Jane's not in danger?

295
00:17:20,618 --> 00:17:21,661
That's absurd.

296
00:17:21,786 --> 00:17:22,954
I'm sorry, agent Abbott

297
00:17:23,079 --> 00:17:24,830
but it is our duty
to protect this man

298
00:17:24,956 --> 00:17:26,499
until we're assured
his safety.

299
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:29,001
Hey. Let him go.

300
00:17:30,127 --> 00:17:31,295
Oh, whoa, whoa.
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

301
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:32,672
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
No, no, no, no, no.

302
00:17:32,797 --> 00:17:34,173
It's all right.
Just stand down.

303
00:17:34,298 --> 00:17:36,968
Stand down, guys. No bloodshed
required. It's cool.

304
00:17:37,969 --> 00:17:39,178
Let him go.

305
00:17:39,554 --> 00:17:40,763
Take my car.

306
00:17:44,892 --> 00:17:45,935
Sir?

307
00:17:46,060 --> 00:17:47,186
It's okay.

308
00:17:50,773 --> 00:17:52,024
Thank you, guys!

309
00:18:04,370 --> 00:18:05,413
We done?

310
00:18:05,538 --> 00:18:06,956
He's gone. We're done.

311
00:18:07,248 --> 00:18:08,291
Hmm.

312
00:18:10,626 --> 00:18:11,669
Arrest them.

313
00:18:12,295 --> 00:18:14,880
Put your guns
down on the ground...

314
00:18:15,631 --> 00:18:16,674
Slowly.

315
00:18:18,050 --> 00:18:19,302
Do as he says.

316
00:18:30,187 --> 00:18:32,815
Go track
agent Lisbon's vehicle.

317
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:33,983
Yes, sir.

318
00:18:34,567 --> 00:18:36,360
You put a bug on my car?

319
00:18:36,736 --> 00:18:38,195
How do you think
we found Jane?

320
00:18:39,572 --> 00:18:41,240
I said I was glad
to see you people

321
00:18:41,365 --> 00:18:42,867
Because I knew you would
screw up

322
00:18:42,992 --> 00:18:44,410
And make my life easy.

323
00:18:44,952 --> 00:18:46,537
And you did just that.

324
00:18:47,330 --> 00:18:48,372
Thank you.

325
00:18:49,332 --> 00:18:50,374
Arrest her.

326
00:18:54,587 --> 00:18:55,630
Come on.

327
00:19:38,422 --> 00:19:39,715
"He wasn't ready for it."

328
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:40,883
"No."

329
00:19:45,471 --> 00:19:48,766
"Yo, yo, yo, yo, yo.
Check it out. Whoa!"

330
00:19:49,308 --> 00:19:50,601
"Check this out."

331
00:19:51,102 --> 00:19:52,144
What's up?

332
00:19:53,062 --> 00:19:55,815
Uh, could you guys keep an eye
on my car for me, please?

333
00:19:56,148 --> 00:19:57,525
Sure, I'll watch it.

334
00:19:57,942 --> 00:19:58,984
Thank you.

335
00:20:02,321 --> 00:20:03,364
Let's go.

336
00:20:05,241 --> 00:20:06,534
Yeah, man, no worries.

337
00:20:12,623 --> 00:20:15,626
"Yeah! Ha ha ha ha!"

338
00:20:35,604 --> 00:20:36,647
Hey there.

339
00:20:40,693 --> 00:20:41,736
Uh...

340
00:20:41,902 --> 00:20:43,195
Sorry to bother you, ma'am.

341
00:20:43,571 --> 00:20:44,780
Uh, long story.

342
00:20:45,156 --> 00:20:47,408
Uh, I need...I need a ride,
if you're willing.

343
00:21:13,476 --> 00:21:15,686
"This is unit 4.
We have the vehicle in sight"

344
00:21:15,811 --> 00:21:17,438
"Stationary
on fifth and Sherman."

345
00:21:18,773 --> 00:21:21,150
Stay back, stay back.
This could be the meet.

346
00:21:24,153 --> 00:21:25,279
"What the heck?"

347
00:21:26,822 --> 00:21:28,365
Unit 4,
what's the situation?

348
00:21:30,868 --> 00:21:32,661
Unit 4, respond, damn it.

349
00:21:33,746 --> 00:21:35,247
"Boss, it was some kids
in Lisbon's car."

350
00:21:35,372 --> 00:21:36,499
"Jane wasn't there."

351
00:21:36,665 --> 00:21:38,959
"We don't have Jane.
Repeat. We don't have Jane."

352
00:21:39,126 --> 00:21:40,169
"Do you co..."

353
00:21:43,714 --> 00:21:45,466
Don't dig yourself
any deeper.

354
00:21:46,342 --> 00:21:47,384
Where'd he go?

355
00:21:47,551 --> 00:21:48,594
I don't know.

356
00:21:51,847 --> 00:21:53,808
You guys really have
a death wish, don't you?

357
00:21:54,016 --> 00:21:55,851
Sir, we really don't know.

358
00:22:04,443 --> 00:22:05,569
Mm-hmm.

359
00:22:10,324 --> 00:22:12,201
"Sir"? Why the hell
are you calling him "sir"?

360
00:22:12,326 --> 00:22:13,828
Oh, calm down, Dillinger.

361
00:22:13,953 --> 00:22:15,704
We're under arrest here.
We might as well be civil.

362
00:22:15,830 --> 00:22:18,207
Why? You think you'll get
a nicer cell?

363
00:22:30,052 --> 00:22:32,555
"Muchas Gracias, Aurelio."

364
00:23:15,389 --> 00:23:16,557
Hey, Patrick.

365
00:23:21,395 --> 00:23:23,355
I'm gonna need to search you
for weapons.

366
00:23:23,606 --> 00:23:25,065
So you can go ahead,
put your hands up.

367
00:23:37,953 --> 00:23:39,204
Worth a shot.

368
00:23:39,705 --> 00:23:40,831
You can go in now.

369
00:23:50,758 --> 00:23:51,800
Patrick.

370
00:23:53,677 --> 00:23:55,137
Thank you for being
so punctual.

371
00:23:57,932 --> 00:23:58,974
You lied to me.

372
00:23:59,099 --> 00:24:01,518
Oh.
Well... as did you.

373
00:24:02,019 --> 00:24:03,938
What a couple of scamps
we are, huh?

374
00:24:05,522 --> 00:24:08,943
I promise that is the last lie
that I will ever tell you.

375
00:24:10,152 --> 00:24:12,571
So...
First things first.

376
00:24:12,738 --> 00:24:15,199
You and the feds have made
a big mistake.

377
00:24:16,575 --> 00:24:17,993
I'm not Red John.

378
00:24:35,302 --> 00:24:36,345
What?

379
00:24:37,846 --> 00:24:39,264
I'm not Red John.

380
00:24:39,848 --> 00:24:41,308
I-I'm sorry to disappoint you

381
00:24:41,433 --> 00:24:42,893
but I'm just
a humble foot soldier

382
00:24:43,018 --> 00:24:44,228
in the Blake association.

383
00:24:44,353 --> 00:24:46,230
Red John is one of
the top brass.

384
00:24:49,900 --> 00:24:51,193
I'm not sure I believe you.

385
00:24:51,443 --> 00:24:54,196
Well...
that's your privilege, but...

386
00:24:54,530 --> 00:24:56,115
But I am telling you the truth.

387
00:24:56,281 --> 00:24:58,325
You all just jumped
to the wrong conclusion.

388
00:25:02,621 --> 00:25:04,415
Okay, so who is
Red John?

389
00:25:04,665 --> 00:25:05,708
Oh, I have no idea.

390
00:25:07,584 --> 00:25:09,044
No, h... honestly.

391
00:25:09,503 --> 00:25:10,546
No idea.

392
00:25:11,714 --> 00:25:14,633
The association works on
a strictly need-to-know basis.

393
00:25:14,967 --> 00:25:16,468
Supposing what you say is true

394
00:25:16,593 --> 00:25:18,595
then we could have had
this talk on the phone.

395
00:25:18,846 --> 00:25:20,514
Yeah, but if we talked
on the phone

396
00:25:20,639 --> 00:25:23,017
then you... you probably
wouldn't have come to meet me

397
00:25:23,142 --> 00:25:24,184
would you?

398
00:25:24,309 --> 00:25:25,728
And I was told to call you

399
00:25:26,186 --> 00:25:29,023
tell you the game's over,
and arrange a meeting.

400
00:25:29,314 --> 00:25:30,357
Why?

401
00:25:31,191 --> 00:25:32,276
Why am I here?

402
00:25:34,945 --> 00:25:38,282
Please... don't think
for a moment

403
00:25:38,407 --> 00:25:40,242
that I am happy about this.

404
00:25:41,201 --> 00:25:43,704
The association doesn't like
loose ends.

405
00:25:44,705 --> 00:25:45,873
Just hates them.

406
00:25:46,540 --> 00:25:47,583
So...

407
00:25:54,131 --> 00:25:55,174
go on, Oscar.

408
00:25:56,759 --> 00:25:58,302
No, no. Listen. Listen.
Let's...

409
00:25:58,427 --> 00:26:00,345
Let's talk about this.
Just... wait.

410
00:26:00,471 --> 00:26:03,599
Now I am truly sorry, but it is
totally out of my hands.

411
00:26:04,641 --> 00:26:06,101
I always liked you, Patrick.

412
00:26:08,187 --> 00:26:10,522
No. No.
This is not necessary.

413
00:26:10,647 --> 00:26:11,815
We don't...don't...

414
00:26:15,069 --> 00:26:16,653
H... hey...

415
00:26:21,075 --> 00:26:22,367
Thank you, Oscar.

416
00:26:24,369 --> 00:26:26,288
You can wait outside.
Just, uh...

417
00:26:27,039 --> 00:26:28,749
make sure we're left
in peace.

418
00:26:38,258 --> 00:26:39,676
Hello, Patrick.

419
00:26:43,347 --> 00:26:44,389
Hi.

420
00:26:59,194 --> 00:27:00,237
Hey!

421
00:27:00,862 --> 00:27:01,947
Hello?!

422
00:27:02,948 --> 00:27:04,407
Hey, what's going on?

423
00:27:04,533 --> 00:27:05,742
- Grace, what are you...
- Hey!

424
00:27:05,867 --> 00:27:07,911
What...please don't
do that.

425
00:27:08,578 --> 00:27:09,621
You're worse than Cho.

426
00:27:09,746 --> 00:27:11,039
They need to tell us
what's going on.

427
00:27:11,206 --> 00:27:12,624
They don't need
to do anything.

428
00:27:13,041 --> 00:27:15,252
And we can't do anything,
so please just relax.

429
00:27:15,377 --> 00:27:17,337
Relax?
How can I relax?

430
00:27:17,462 --> 00:27:19,131
You know, sometimes I think
you like being helpless.

431
00:27:19,256 --> 00:27:20,924
Okay, fine, I take it back.
Don't relax.

432
00:27:21,049 --> 00:27:22,092
Just break the window
with your forehead

433
00:27:22,217 --> 00:27:23,385
and we'll all jump out
and make a run for it.

434
00:27:23,510 --> 00:27:25,470
Guys, let's try to keep it
together, okay?

435
00:27:25,595 --> 00:27:26,888
Okay, I'm sorry.

436
00:27:29,015 --> 00:27:30,058
"Sorry."

437
00:27:32,894 --> 00:27:34,312
Mullins,
you're from here, yes?

438
00:27:34,437 --> 00:27:35,564
Yes, sir. Over to Lincoln heights.

439
00:27:35,689 --> 00:27:37,440
- Get me a map of Sacramento.
- Yes, sir.

440
00:27:37,566 --> 00:27:38,900
There's one on the computer
in the car.

441
00:27:39,234 --> 00:27:40,277
Paper map.

442
00:27:42,696 --> 00:27:44,239
Paper... map.

443
00:27:44,906 --> 00:27:45,991
Come on. Let's go.

444
00:27:48,743 --> 00:27:50,120
Hey, do you have a paper map?

445
00:27:51,329 --> 00:27:53,915
Well, Patrick, here we are.

446
00:27:58,420 --> 00:27:59,671
Poor fella.

447
00:28:00,505 --> 00:28:01,965
Smart but dumb.

448
00:28:04,342 --> 00:28:05,468
It never occurred to him

449
00:28:05,594 --> 00:28:08,180
that I am
the Blake association.

450
00:28:08,638 --> 00:28:09,890
Why'd you have to kill him?

451
00:28:11,892 --> 00:28:13,685
Everyone thinks
he's Red John, don't they?

452
00:28:14,144 --> 00:28:16,855
So... It would seem
a fitting end to the story

453
00:28:16,980 --> 00:28:19,274
if you two were found dead
together.

454
00:28:20,317 --> 00:28:21,735
No one will look
any deeper.

455
00:28:21,860 --> 00:28:23,612
So I'm supposed to die,
am I?

456
00:28:24,821 --> 00:28:26,406
After all these years

457
00:28:27,032 --> 00:28:28,450
seems kind of unfair.

458
00:28:28,992 --> 00:28:30,327
It's totally fair.

459
00:28:30,493 --> 00:28:32,078
The game's over,
and I won.

460
00:28:32,954 --> 00:28:33,997
It's not a game.

461
00:28:35,248 --> 00:28:36,875
There's a winner and a loser.
That's a game.

462
00:28:37,417 --> 00:28:38,960
It's not a game I asked to play.

463
00:28:39,294 --> 00:28:41,213
No, but you played it
very well nonetheless.

464
00:28:41,546 --> 00:28:44,216
You were fun, challenging.
Thank you.

465
00:28:48,762 --> 00:28:50,597
You probably have a lot
of questions for me, huh?

466
00:28:51,806 --> 00:28:53,141
We have time, if you want.

467
00:28:53,767 --> 00:28:54,976
I have no questions.

468
00:28:56,144 --> 00:28:58,605
You're an evil,
sexually perverted sociopath

469
00:28:58,730 --> 00:29:00,690
with pathetic delusions
of grandeur.

470
00:29:01,566 --> 00:29:03,151
The rest is just details.

471
00:29:04,152 --> 00:29:07,197
"Evil, sexually perverted sociopath"?

472
00:29:08,949 --> 00:29:11,660
Well, I guess I have to
own that, but, uh...

473
00:29:12,327 --> 00:29:14,246
"delusions of grandeur"?

474
00:29:15,497 --> 00:29:16,539
No.

475
00:29:17,082 --> 00:29:18,833
I have no delusions.

476
00:29:20,585 --> 00:29:22,128
I built a secret empire.

477
00:29:22,254 --> 00:29:24,965
I control the lives
of thousands of people.

478
00:29:25,131 --> 00:29:26,758
My word is life and death

479
00:29:26,967 --> 00:29:28,009
and nobody knows who I am.

480
00:29:28,218 --> 00:29:30,053
Now if that's not grandeur

481
00:29:30,220 --> 00:29:31,388
I don't know
what you call it.

482
00:29:32,055 --> 00:29:35,100
I'd call it the ravings
of a squalid egomaniac.

483
00:29:36,977 --> 00:29:38,019
You see?

484
00:29:38,436 --> 00:29:42,565
For no reason at all, you...
You're rude and contemptuous.

485
00:29:44,067 --> 00:29:46,444
That's why your wife
and kid are dead.

486
00:29:47,779 --> 00:29:49,864
Who are you to butt in here

487
00:29:49,990 --> 00:29:52,742
and make obnoxious
judgments about me?

488
00:29:54,744 --> 00:29:55,829
Who are you?

489
00:29:57,455 --> 00:29:58,498
Who are you?

490
00:30:00,667 --> 00:30:01,710
Nobody.

491
00:30:03,128 --> 00:30:04,170
Nobody.

492
00:30:04,879 --> 00:30:06,339
You didn't know me.

493
00:30:06,631 --> 00:30:07,966
You don't know me.

494
00:30:08,633 --> 00:30:10,051
You have no idea.

495
00:30:13,346 --> 00:30:14,639
Here's your problem, Pat.

496
00:30:15,557 --> 00:30:18,393
You're a smart man,
but you are arrogant.

497
00:30:19,561 --> 00:30:21,855
You can't imagine someone
smarter than you.

498
00:30:22,814 --> 00:30:23,857
Which is why I've been
ahead of you

499
00:30:23,982 --> 00:30:25,275
at every step along the way.

500
00:30:26,234 --> 00:30:28,403
You're holding the gun.
You wanna brag?

501
00:30:28,611 --> 00:30:30,280
Go ahead.
I'm not gonna stop you.

502
00:30:34,159 --> 00:30:35,744
You still don't know
how I fooled you, do you?

503
00:30:37,037 --> 00:30:38,997
How did I survive
that bomb?

504
00:30:40,540 --> 00:30:42,834
How did I know all the names
on your list?

505
00:30:43,626 --> 00:30:46,588
Is this what you've been missing?
Appreciation?

506
00:30:46,796 --> 00:30:47,839
Hmm?

507
00:30:48,256 --> 00:30:49,674
Do you want me to applaud?

508
00:30:50,508 --> 00:30:52,594
You have no idea, do you?

509
00:30:53,011 --> 00:30:55,305
I don't know how you got
the list of suspects.

510
00:30:55,680 --> 00:30:56,931
That was a good trick.

511
00:30:58,350 --> 00:31:00,185
But the bomb gag is simple.

512
00:31:00,560 --> 00:31:01,603
There were two explosions.

513
00:31:01,728 --> 00:31:03,813
The first was a concussion bomb,
knocked everyone out.

514
00:31:03,938 --> 00:31:07,650
The second, lethal bomb
that Killed Haffner and stiles

515
00:31:07,776 --> 00:31:10,737
only went off after you
dragged Bertram, Smith, and me

516
00:31:10,862 --> 00:31:12,155
out of harm's way.

517
00:31:12,489 --> 00:31:13,656
Correct.

518
00:31:15,283 --> 00:31:17,202
Faking your own death
was easy.

519
00:31:17,827 --> 00:31:19,746
Brett Partridge was
Blake association.

520
00:31:20,080 --> 00:31:21,790
His job gave him access

521
00:31:21,915 --> 00:31:24,167
To the primary
DNA database.

522
00:31:24,584 --> 00:31:26,086
He switched
your DNA records

523
00:31:26,211 --> 00:31:28,630
With a body
that you had on ice.

524
00:31:29,297 --> 00:31:30,548
A surrogate.

525
00:31:31,257 --> 00:31:32,675
